{"version": 2, "width": 96, "height": 22, "title": "Does your heap dump contain your database password?"}
[0.01, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ ./demo/heap-dump/run.sh jars\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.014, "o", "\u001b[1m-> PostgreSQL 17 and a Vault dev server; the database password lives in Vault\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.729, "o", "\u001b[1m-> the same application twice: pgjdbc and seclume, both reading the password from Vault\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.678, "o", "\u001b[1m-> both connected; now a heap dump of each JVM, searched for the password and the token\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.897, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m== pgjdbc - the password from Vault as a String\u001b[0m\r\n  database password:\r\n"]
[9.607, "o", "    \u001b[1;31mFOUND\u001b[0m - the secret is in the heap of process 26, 2 time(s):\r\n      raw file: UTF-8 match of 31 bytes at 9168916\r\n      byte[] 30309483496: UTF-8 match of 31 bytes at 132\r\n"]
[9.608, "o", "  Vault token:\r\n"]
[10.077, "o", "    \u001b[1;31mFOUND\u001b[0m - the secret is in the heap of process 26, 2 time(s):\r\n      raw file: UTF-8 match of 30 bytes at 9461403\r\n      byte[] 30309697664: UTF-8 match of 30 bytes at 0\r\n"]
[10.077, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m== seclume - the password from Vault into native memory\u001b[0m\r\n  database password:\r\n"]
[10.774, "o", "    \u001b[1;32mNOT FOUND\u001b[0m - the secret from /shared/db-password is not in the heap of process 46.\r\n"]
[10.774, "o", "  Vault token:\r\n"]
[11.224, "o", "    \u001b[1;32mNOT FOUND\u001b[0m - the secret from /shared/vault-token is not in the heap of process 46.\r\n"]
[14.224, "o", ""]
